==English==

===Etymology===
{{lbor|en|la-lat|repertōrium}}. {{dbt|en|repertoire}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɹɛp.əɹˌtɔɹ.i/|/ˈɹɛpəɹˌtoʊɹ.i/|a=GA}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɹɛpətɹi/|a=RP}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-repertory.wav|a=Southern England}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[repertoire]].
# A [[collection]] of things, or a place where such a collection is kept.
# A specific set of [[work]]s that a [[company]] [[perform]]s.
# A [[theater]] in which a [[resident]] company presents [[work]]s from a specified [[repertoire]], usually in alternation.
# {{lb|en|chiefly|_|attributive}} A [[cinema]] specializing in [[classic]] or older films.

